From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:37:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 081/112] LPF: the 12 / 24 dB ladders sing on their own from
 the same resonance and as loud as in the original firmware again

- Below tannedFrequency 6000000 (about 310 Hz) the resonance goes down again, by up to 9 % at the bottom, as in the
  original firmware (fc76a9cd filter_set_config.cpp). Community #304 (aa3d0bc7) lost this, so at low cutoff the ladder
  self-oscillated from lower resonance and louder (the 32 Hz hum in "New Sitar Grii 10").
- The 12 dB and 24 dB ladders saturate per context as in the original: 2 in voices, 3 in the song's, a kit's and an
  audio track's filters (community #336 made it 2 everywhere: 6 dB louder self-oscillation there). The drive ladder
  and morph below the saturating resonance are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
